course: dictionary
lesson: 7830
title: Quotations and quotation marks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quotation is a set of words copied exactly from a book, a speech or a person. We show them with quotation marks. «"To be or not to be" is a famous quotation.» The marks tell you these are someone else's exact words.
explain: Quotation has another meaning too. It is a price that a builder or company says a job will cost, which is a quote. «The quotation for painting the fence is $240.» If you get several quotations, compare them to find the cheapest.
explain: Quotation marks can also show that a word is not meant literally. «But every night he left the hall light on "by accident".» The quotation marks tell you it wasn't an accident at all. Always read the marks as a clue to the meaning.
fact: A quotation is words copied exactly from a book, speech or person.
fact: A quotation can also be a price a builder or company says a job will cost.
fact: Quotation marks are the signs ' ' or " " put around spoken or copied words.
fact: Quotation marks can show that a word is not meant literally, as in «by accident» when it was on purpose.
exercise: In «"To be or not to be" is a famous quotation», what is the quotation? | A price for painting a fence | *The exact words copied from a famous play | The signs ' ' or " " | A short story about a hall light
exercise: The builder says «The quotation for painting the fence is $240.» What does quotation mean here? | *A price the builder says the job will cost | A promise to paint the fence for free | The marks put around spoken words | Words copied exactly from a book
exercise: What are quotation marks? | A long sentence with no full stops | A type of book | Lines drawn under a title | *The signs ' ' or " " put around spoken or copied words
test: In «But every night he left the hall light on "by accident".», what do the quotation marks tell you? | The hall was dark | It was an accident after all | *It was not an accident at all, it was on purpose | The light was broken
test: Which of these is a quotation? | A list of cheap builders | A price a company asks for a job | *Words copied exactly from a famous speech | The quotation marks on a page
exam: Which word means the same as quotation when it means a price? | A question | *A quote | A quiet voice | A quarter
